# Push and restart after completed work

**Exception: scheduled or automated agents.** If you are running as an automation (for example the ChessX Town builder), or you were told to work on an `agent/*` branch, this rule does NOT apply. Push only your own `agent/*` branch, open a pull request, and stop. Never run `deploy.sh`, never ssh to the droplet, never push to or merge into `main` or the base branch. Only the owner deploys.

When a task is finished (feature, fix, or other code change the user asked for):

1. Commit any uncommitted work if it is not already committed (only the files for that task).
2. Push the current branch to `origin` (`git push -u origin HEAD` if it has no upstream).
3. Restart production on the DigitalOcean droplet:
   `ssh -i $HOME/.ssh/aibot_do_ed25519 root@159.223.115.153 "/opt/chessx/deploy/deploy.sh"`
4. Report the commit, that the push landed, and that the container is up.

Do this without being asked again. Skip only if there is nothing to ship (no code changes).
